ggml-cuda: per (architecture, type, rows) table for the dequant + BF16 cuBLAS route; sm75 FP16 prototype

Patch 0016 sent only Q8_0 to dequant + BF16 cuBLAS (sm80 / sm90 / sm100 from 1024 rows, sm120 from 4096) and kept
every K-quant on MMQ. Measured on sd.cpp renders (FLUX.2 klein 4B, FLUX.3 klein, Z-Image Turbo, Qwen-Image 2.1
Turbo; steady s/step, 3 interleaved repeats, 512 and 1024 px):
  A100 (sm80): Q4_K_M / Q5_K_M / Q6_K files 1.90-2.21x faster per step on cuBLAS at 1024 px, 1.67-1.73x at 512 px.
  RTX PRO 6000 (sm120): Q6_K 1.20x at 1024 px and 1.04-1.12x at 512 px; Q4_K alone 1.015-1.11x and Q5_K alone
  1.03-1.05x from 4096 rows, both slower below that, so they start at 4096.
  L4 (sm89): Q6_K 1.04-1.06x at 1024 px; Q4_K / Q5_K tie or lose, Q8_0 loses 5-6%, so only Q6_K moves.
  LPIPS vs the BF16 / F16 GGUF render of the same seed: mean lower on cuBLAS in most (card, model, type) cells,
  higher by at most 0.004 (inside the per-seed spread) in the rest.
The policy moves into src/ggml-cuda/quant-route.h (host-only, checked by scripts/quant_route_table_test.cpp in
stable-diffusion.cpp). sm86 / sm87 / sm90 / sm100 / sm121 K-quants are unmeasured and keep MMQ; Q8_0 is unchanged
everywhere.

Env: GGML_CUDA_QUANT_CUBLAS_MIN_BATCH=<rows> still overrides every quantized type (0 = MMQ everywhere);
GGML_CUDA_QUANT_CUBLAS_TYPES=q4_K,q6_K limits that override to the listed types; GGML_CUDA_QUANT_ROUTE_LOG=1 logs each
(type, route) the first time it runs. GGML_CUDA_QUANT_CUBLAS_F16=<rows> (off by default) is a Turing prototype:
dequant to FP16 and cuBLAS with FP16 inputs and FP32 accumulate / output, since sm75 has no BF16 tensor cores
(T4: 1.05-1.20x per step on FLUX.2 klein 4B and Z-Image Turbo K-quant / Q8_0 files, LPIPS unchanged).

